WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:06.590
The hotly-anticipated Shadow and Bone introduces
the lavish fantasy world of the Grishaverse

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:11.280
from dark villains to chosen ones, shadow
monsters to magical maguffins, and a charismatic

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.790
crew of hustlers thrown in for good measure.

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:17.820
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm breaking down everything you

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:22.279
need to know about Shadow and Bone, that final
shot of the Darkling, and all the clues to

00:00:22.279 --> 00:00:25.589
what you can expect in Season 2 for Alina,
Mal and the Crows.

00:00:25.589 --> 00:00:28.550
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:33.329
Dominating the world of Shadow and Bone is
the Fold, a giant area of darkness created

00:00:33.329 --> 00:00:37.399
by The Darkling hundreds of years before the
main events of the show and which split the

00:00:37.399 --> 00:00:39.640
powerful nation of Ravka in two.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:44.449
At the time, The Darkling was the Ravkan king's
military advisor and had used his Grisha powers

00:00:44.449 --> 00:00:46.150
to help the king win a war.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:50.109
However when the king became fearful of the
Darkling's desire for more power, he put a

00:00:50.109 --> 00:00:51.490
bounty on his head.

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:55.780
After the king's soldiers finally tracked
down the Darkling, he turned to a form of

00:00:55.780 --> 00:01:00.850
forbidden magic known as merzost once used
by his forefather Ilya Morozova.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:05.320
The Grisha only practice the Small Science,
which they define as the manipulation of matter

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:09.050
which already exists,
and because it doesn't involve conjuring or

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:13.460
creating something from nothing, they don't
consider it magic strictly speaking.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:18.340
The use of merzost for the work of creation
on the other hand is much more dangerous and

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:21.060
unstable;
so although the Darkling's intention was only

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:25.570
to transform the king's soldiers into his
own army, he lost control of the magic and

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:27.720
ended up creating the Shadow Fold.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:31.840
As the merzost escaped it transformed the
ordinary human beings who lived in the area

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:36.430
of the Fold into monsters known as volcra
which now roam the shadow world threatening

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:40.600
and attacking anyone who enters or attempts
to pass through.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:44.770
Several hundred years later in the present
time of the show, the Darkling who now goes

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:50.110
by the name General Kirigan, leads Ravka's
Second Army which is made up entirely of Grisha.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:55.530
Although he appeared to create the Fold accidentally,
its existence has made Ravka dependent on

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:59.740
the Grisha and their powers to help traverse
the dangerous routes through the Fold.

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:02.860
"Bide your time until there's a problem only
Grisha can solve.

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:04.600
Then the King must embrace us."

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:09.950
So, when Alina Starkov discovers her Sun Summoner
powers with the ability to destroy volcra,

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:12.260
Kirigan takes a special interest in her.

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:16.090
He takes her to the Little Palace to train
and develop her powers which she was unaware

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:17.260
existed.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:22.340
Kirigan claims he wants to use her to help
destroy the Fold and free Ravka from its curse.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:27.580
At the palace, Alina ends up becoming romantically
interested in Kirigan until his mother Baghra

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:32.560
reveals the truth about who he really is and
explains he's obsessed with finding Morozova's

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.200
stag,
a potent amplifier that will increase his

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.060
power dramatically.

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:41.480
Alina flees and, after a brief encounter with
the Crows, she ends up reuniting with Mal

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:43.840
and together they track down the stag themselves.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:48.680
Ever since she was a child, Alina has had
dreams of the stag and we can see the connection

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:53.070
she has with the magical animal when she touches
it and it amplifies her power.

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:56.900
Kirigan and his Grisha, however, interrupt
this moment and he kills the poor creature

00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:00.560
with the Cut, the lethal blade he can summon
from darkness.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:05.510
Kirigan then has David perform a bonding ritual
that fuses the stag's antlers onto Alina's

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:10.180
body while tethering her to Kirigan giving
him control over her powers and the ability

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:12.000
to turn them on and off as he pleases.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.930
"You could've made me your equal.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:15.540
Instead, you made me this."

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:20.290
With Alina under his control, Kirigan puts
into motion the final step of his plan and

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:25.000
uses her Sun Summoner powers to create a safe
tunnel for him and a group of foreign emissaries

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.970
to travel through the Fold.

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:31.020
Alina then asks Kirigan to use her to destroy
the fold as he once said he would.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:32.780
"Why would we destroy the Fold?

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.810
It's the greatest weapon that we've got."

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:39.570
In a lethal demonstration of the power he
now wields, he expands the Shadow Fold beyond

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:44.870
its current position to consume the city of
Novokribirsk right on the Fold's borders.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:49.870
As the darkness and volcra consume the city,
Kirigan rids himself of General Zlatan, the

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:55.810
Western Ravkan independence leader who threatened
the unity of Ravka and ordered Alina's assassination.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:04:00.310
With this gruesome display of power, Kirigan
demands the foreign ambassadors on the skiff

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:03.280
submit to his demands to end their wars with
Ravka.

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:08.730
"With the power of the Sun Summoner at my
command, I control the Fold.

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:09.730
And its monsters.

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:10.730
I can move it to any border I like.

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:12.650
All countries will answer to us."

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:17.629
Mal and the Crows intervene, with Inej almost
killing Kirigan as she shoots a knife into

00:04:17.629 --> 00:04:18.629
his chest.

00:04:18.629 --> 00:04:23.069
The Darkling, however, calls on his merzost
powers, which seem to be one of the reasons

00:04:23.069 --> 00:04:26.970
he's immortal, and pulls out the knife, tossing
it aside.

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:31.199
Alina then has a vision of Morozova's stag
again, and seeing the knife to her side she

00:04:31.199 --> 00:04:35.800
uses it to stab Kirigan through the hand,
which slices off the wedge of skin melded

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:38.430
onto his wrist that was keeping her tethered
to him.

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:43.770
It's a striking moment as Alina regains autonomy
over both her own body and her abilities as

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:44.770
the Sun Summoner.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:48.919
"Your first words to me were,
'What are you?'

00:04:48.919 --> 00:04:52.409
This is what I am."

00:04:52.409 --> 00:04:57.150
Kirigan can't understand how Alina now has
control over the amplifier because he killed

00:04:57.150 --> 00:05:02.129
the stag so says he should have control over
it, which is what the legends about Morozova's

00:05:02.129 --> 00:05:03.240
creatures say.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:07.169
"They learned killing one of these beasts
and then melding a piece of it into their

00:05:07.169 --> 00:05:09.729
body would amplify their abilities."

00:05:09.729 --> 00:05:13.270
Alina explains though that it was the stag's
choice to give her the power.

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:17.490
This is presumably down to Alina's connection
with the stag she'd already established throughout

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:21.669
her life and perhaps the fact she chose not
to kill the animal when she found it.

00:05:21.669 --> 00:05:24.509
"I didn't understand before, but I do now.

00:05:24.509 --> 00:05:26.520
You cannot claim what was not given to you.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:28.319
The Stag chose me."

00:05:28.319 --> 00:05:32.509
Proving her point, the antlers which until
then had been crudely melded onto her body

00:05:32.509 --> 00:05:36.589
are now absorbed into her as the stag seems
to become one with Alina,

00:05:36.589 --> 00:05:41.090
a convenient practical detail when it comes
to prosthetics and VFX for future seasons

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:42.350
of the show as well.

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:46.539
This isn't the last we've seen of Morozova's
amplifiers though and there are at least two

00:05:46.539 --> 00:05:48.120
more to appear in future seasons.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:50.839
More on those very shortly.

00:05:50.839 --> 00:05:54.879
Kirigan is still alive, of course, and although
he ends up hauled off by a Volcra during his

00:05:54.879 --> 00:05:58.369
fight with Mal,
the final shot of the season reveals he survived

00:05:58.369 --> 00:06:03.180
this, something not that surprising given
his own mother described him as "eternal".

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:07.249
We can see he's been wounded badly with some
deep scars on his face, though I'm sure he

00:06:07.249 --> 00:06:09.940
could find a Grisha Healer for these at some
point;

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:15.439
but, more significantly, emerging from the
Fold are some new evil-looking shadow creatures.

00:06:15.439 --> 00:06:19.779
These are Nichevo'ya, also known as "nothings"
and are another creation of the Darkling's

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:20.879
merzost powers.

00:06:20.879 --> 00:06:25.900
They are a different kind of beast to the
volcra as they can pass outside the Fold and

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:29.780
I expect we'll see Kirigan use these monsters
against Alina and Mal when he tracks them

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:32.129
down in Season 2.

00:06:32.129 --> 00:06:37.349
Unaware that Kirigan is still alive, Alina,
Mal, the Crows, and Zoya plan their next steps.

00:06:37.349 --> 00:06:40.309
Alina is concerned she'll be blamed for the
destruction of Novokribirsk

00:06:40.309 --> 00:06:43.999
and Zoya says the Apparat who's now pulling
the strings at the royal palace since the

00:06:43.999 --> 00:06:49.289
king's poisoning will blame everything on
the Grisha again and asks Alina to find new

00:06:49.289 --> 00:06:50.289
allies.

00:06:50.289 --> 00:06:54.409
This is setting up Season 2 of Alina's storyline
which, if it stays close to the books more

00:06:54.409 --> 00:06:57.990
or less like the first season,
should see Alina and Mal travel across the

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:02.969
True Sea in search of another of Morozova's
amplifiers that Alina already learned about

00:07:02.969 --> 00:07:05.020
from the Apparat earlier in the show.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:06.340
"It all began with this man.

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:08.729
One of the first Grisha in recorded history.

00:07:08.729 --> 00:07:09.729
The Bonesmith."

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:14.499
Book readers will know that the Bonesmith's
real name is Ilya Morozova, who was Baghra's

00:07:14.499 --> 00:07:17.689
father and therefore the Darkling's grandfather.

00:07:17.689 --> 00:07:22.280
The Bonesmith was obsessed with creating amplifiers
that could boost a Grisha's powers as the

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:23.520
Apparat explains.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:28.789
"He made creatures from his own finger bones.

00:07:28.789 --> 00:07:31.680
Mythical animals brimming with power.

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.529
Attuned only to Grisha."

00:07:33.529 --> 00:07:38.449
We can see Morozova's Stag on this page, the
first amplifier that Alina has already acquired,

00:07:38.449 --> 00:07:42.559
but there are two other important creatures,
the Sea Whip and the Firebird, that we can

00:07:42.559 --> 00:07:45.479
expect to show up in subsequent seasons of
the show.

00:07:45.479 --> 00:07:49.970
The Sea Whip, like the stag, is a legendary
beast from Ravkan folklore and is said to

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:54.629
be a dragon prince cursed to live as a sea
serpent in waters known as the Bone Road.

00:07:54.629 --> 00:07:58.682
We got a hint that Alina will be headed to
those icy waters in Season 2 in one of the

00:07:58.682 --> 00:08:00.150
books she picks up at the library.

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:03.349
"The bone road ebbs and the bone road flows."

00:08:03.349 --> 00:08:07.439
Once caught or killed, the Sea Whip's scales
can be used to create a fetter or a bracelet

00:08:07.439 --> 00:08:11.139
that when worn around the wrist will amplify
a Grisha's powers.

00:08:11.139 --> 00:08:15.490
Notice how Alina turns her wrist in this same
scene, foreshadowing the second amplifier

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:18.319
that we can expect to see her wear in Season
2.

00:08:18.319 --> 00:08:22.669
The third amplifier that Morozova is said
to have created is the Firebird, something

00:08:22.669 --> 00:08:25.860
that probably won't be seen until a third
season or later.

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:29.800
However, there is another possible living
amplifier that the show may already be hiding

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:32.729
in plain sight:
Alina's childhood friend Mal.

00:08:32.729 --> 00:08:36.750
There've been several scenes hinting that
Mal may have some latent powers and that he's

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:39.880
even more crucial to Alina's destiny than
we might imagine.

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:44.620
Although everyone including Mal seems to assume
he's not Grisha, we know he wasn't tested

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:48.839
on the day the Grisha came to the orphanage
because he was injured, so we don't have conclusive

00:08:48.839 --> 00:08:50.300
proof about that.

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:54.360
And if you re-watch carefully the scene when
Alina discovers her Sun Summoner powers for

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:57.850
the first time, this occurs while she's holding
hands with Mal.

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:01.839
Which is, of course, similar to how Kirigan
helped Alina activate her power by taking

00:09:01.839 --> 00:09:05.990
hold of her hand when she was at the Ravkan
court to demonstrate her abilities.

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:10.080
From that scene we know that Kirigan is a
living amplifier, which suggests that Mal

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:15.360
may be one too and that it was his touch which
activated Alina's powers for the first time.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:19.089
Notice also how Mal and Alina hold hands as
children when they're hiding together to avoid

00:09:19.089 --> 00:09:22.290
doing the Grisha test,
and then at the end of the second episode

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:25.800
there's a moment where the pair seem to be
able to sense each other even though they're

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:27.230
miles apart.

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:31.529
That sixth sense and connection with Alina
seems to be what helps him find Morozova's

00:09:31.529 --> 00:09:34.750
Stag when he's tracking it, as he explains
in the letter he writes to her during his

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:36.889
expedition to find the mythical creature.

00:09:36.889 --> 00:09:39.329
"When you lit up Kirigan's tent, there was
a sound.

00:09:39.329 --> 00:09:40.329
A high tone.

00:09:40.329 --> 00:09:41.329
I knew it was you...

00:09:41.329 --> 00:09:44.839
When we were kids, you'd hold my hand and
sometimes I'd hear it in the back of my head.

00:09:44.839 --> 00:09:47.810
Then I hear that sound again.

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:48.810
Softly.

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:49.810
Calling to me."

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:54.329
The show is clearly hinting that there's something
particularly special about Mal's tracking

00:09:54.329 --> 00:09:58.130
abilities, which I expect we'll see him use
to find the Sea Whip in Season 2.

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:02.519
And, by the way, if Mal truly does have a
special connection with Morozova's amplifiers,

00:10:02.519 --> 00:10:06.290
it implies there's a lot more to his past
and his heritage than his orphanage upbringing

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:07.459
might suggest.

00:10:07.459 --> 00:10:10.790
I'll talk more about some other easter eggs
you might have missed in the first season

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:12.110
in my next Shadow and Bone video.

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:15.690
I'll add a link here and in the video description
as soon as it's ready.

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:20.629
Of course, we also have to talk about the
Crows, Kaz, Inej and Jesper, who in the book

00:10:20.629 --> 00:10:25.230
Grishaverse don't show up until a few years
after the main events of the Shadow and Bone

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:26.230
trilogy.

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:30.199
What the TV show has done therefore is to
create a prequel story for the Crows characters

00:10:30.199 --> 00:10:34.990
in which we discover they were involved in
an attempted heist to kidnap the Sun Summoner.

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:39.069
That obviously didn't work out for them, however,
they leave Alina and Mal on good enough terms

00:10:39.069 --> 00:10:42.510
at the end and although their paths don't
cross in the book Grishaverse,

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:47.279
as the TV show is its own thing, we may well
see them meet again in the future.

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:50.670
What we do know is that at the end of the
first season, the Crows are heading back to

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:53.990
Ketterdam where both Dreesen and Pekka Rollins
await them.

00:10:53.990 --> 00:10:58.190
Kaz says he has a plan for dealing with them
that requires a Heartrender and, what are

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:02.720
the chances but, sitting right by them and
overhearing their conversation is Nina, a

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:04.690
Grisha with that exact skillset.

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:07.690
Nina is on the boat with her former enemy-turned-lover
Matthias,

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:12.980
who's in chains now and destined for the Hellgate
prison in Ketterdam after Nina found herself

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:17.230
forced to accuse him of being a slaver so
he wouldn't be taken away by the Grisha.

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:22.110
In the Six of Crows book, Kaz, Inej, Jesper
and Nina team up together with another character

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:26.730
we haven't seen yet called Wylan for a heist
to break out a scientist being held prisoner

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:27.730
in Fjerda.

00:11:27.730 --> 00:11:32.180
In the novel, they also need Matthias to do
this, so break him out of Hellgate prison.

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:36.660
Assuming then the show at least roughly follows
the plot of the Six of Crows duology, we can

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:39.399
expect to see him reunited with Nina.

00:11:39.399 --> 00:11:43.620
Showrunner Eric Heisserer and Grishaverse
author Leigh Bardugo, who's a producer on

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:46.490
the show,
at the time of making this video haven't confirmed

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:50.440
whether they'll continue to combine the Crows
ongoing storyline with the Shadow and Bone

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:54.420
characters in future seasons,
or whether the Crows could get their own separate

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:56.699
spin-off show set in the same universe.

00:11:56.699 --> 00:11:59.180
"You stick with us, everybody gets what they
want."

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:03.610
Either way, I think the Crows will be a hit
with fans thanks to the heist action and humour

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:04.740
they bring to the story.

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:05.740
"So... what did we learn?

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:06.760
People with trains are evil.

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:09.339
You can't kidnap a human sunbeam.

00:12:09.339 --> 00:12:12.700
True wealth is the friends you make along
the way."

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:15.660
So what did you think of the first season
of Shadow and Bone?

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:18.400
And do you have any theories on what will
happen next?

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:22.720
Comment with your thoughts below, and if you
enjoyed this, then a thumbs-up would be hugely

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:23.720
appreciated.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:27.319
And you can tap left to discover all the easter
eggs and book connections you might have missed

00:12:27.319 --> 00:12:31.279
in Season 1 or tap right for something else
you're sure to like.

00:12:31.279 --> 00:12:33.050
Thanks for watching and see ya next time!

00:12:33.050 --> 00:12:34.589
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

